From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:45:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: push constant-offset dynamic UBO reads of fragment
 shaders to the FAU

DXVK binds every D3D constant buffer as a dynamic uniform buffer, and its
fragment shaders read the constants at constant offsets. PanVK marked no UBO
pushable, so each read was an LD_PKA through the load/store unit; Portal 2's
fragment shaders spend 4-10 load/store cycles each against under one cycle of
arithmetic.

Mark the dynamic uniform buffers of fragment shaders pushable: the compiler's
bi_opt_push_ubo moves their constant-offset reads into the FAU and records
the pushed words as relocations (UBO, offset) in the FAU layout. At each draw
the vertex/tiler command stream copies those words from the bound buffer
(address and dynamic offset are known when recording) into the draw's FAU
block, so they are read when the draw executes, like the loads they replace.
Words past the bound range read as zero. Every draw with pushed words gets a
new FAU block: earlier draws' fragment jobs may still read theirs. The loads
are batched in the 14 data registers v11's CS scratch range leaves.

Compiler: only resource table 0 handles are pushable (UBOs live there for
both drivers), the analysis covers every pushable index, and drivers without
a blend-constant sysval UBO (PanVK) skip those reserved slots.

Vertex shaders stay as they are: a D3D9 vertex shader pushes dozens of vec4s,
and copying them for every draw costs more than the loads (Portal 2 184 ->
150 fps, Tomb Raider 74.9 -> 71.5). PANVK_NO_UBO_PUSH=1 keeps all reads as
loads.

Portal 2: load/store read issues per frame -70%, attribute unit instructions
-71%, 169.5/171.0 -> 174.5/172.3 fps. Tomb Raider (2013) benchmark: 73.0/72.5
-> 75.3/74.9 fps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: D3D performance: constant-offset reads of dynamic uniform buffers (DXVK's D3D constant buffers) in fragment shaders become FAU uniform reads instead of LD_PKA loads; the vertex/tiler command stream copies the pushed words from the bound buffer into each draw's FAU block at execution time
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: applies after rg477m/048
Validation test: test build push2 (same code with a vertex-shader test switch): PanProbe 38/38 x2; Portal 2 (D3D9, DXVK 1.10.9) gameplay A-B-B-A 169.5/171.0 -> 174.5/172.3 fps, load/store read issues per frame -70%, attribute unit instructions -71%, correct rendering; Tomb Raider (2013) benchmark (DXVK 1.11.1) 73.0/72.5 -> 75.3/74.9 fps; vkd3d-proton 2.14.1 suite 309 PASS, same set as 001-048 (B27 flake aside); gameplay A/B vs 001-048: Hades hub 223.6 vs 223.2, Jupiter Hell 48.7 vs 48.6, Risk of Rain 2 28.8 vs 27.9 (noise); Arkham Asylum 20 interleaved rounds 35.5 vs 35.5 fps, load failures (B5 family) 3/20 base vs 2/20; 16-game boot sweep: every game in its known state, no GPU faults; vertex-shader push measured slower (Portal 2 184 -> 150, Tomb Raider 74.9 -> 71.5) and left out; opt-out PANVK_NO_UBO_PUSH=1
